caption: HyperGSD List Widget
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]
title: hgsd.list widget

The `$hgsd.list` widget is the single list engine behind every dashboard and reusable list block. It takes an arbitrary filter, applies the realm system's four-case set arithmetic, freezes itself against the global refresh cycle, and renders rows composed from the [[ListItem|ListItem Prefix and Suffix]] tags. Start filters with `tag[]` rather than an explicit `all[tiddlers]` — the default source carries the tag index, so a leading `tag[]` reads it directly, while an explicit prefix forces a full-wiki scan per evaluation.

! Content and Attributes

|>|>| !<$hgsd.list> |
| !Attribute | !Default | !Description |
|list-heading |— |Heading shown on the collapsible list block. |
|list-filter |— |''Required.'' Any filter over tiddler titles; the widget applies realm scoping to its output. Drafts never list — the widget excludes them from the filter output (they inherit the base tiddler's fields and would otherwise appear mid-edit). |
|group-by |(blank) |Field to group rows by (e.g. `gsd_project`). Blank renders a flat list. |
|group-state |`false` |`false` renders flat; any other value renders grouped (legacy fixed grouping — the contexts view's lists use it). |
|group-select |`no` |`yes` renders the grouping strip under the heading: a radio per `$:/tags/hypergsd/GroupBy` dimension (leading None = flat) plus an include-ungrouped checkbox. While no dimension is offered (all withdrawn, or nothing type-relevant) the whole Group by block — None included — withdraws, and without `sort-select` the strip row itself goes. |
|group-members |(blank) |Filter whose output replaces the offered dimension set outright (type relevance deliberately skipped). |
|sort-select |`no` |`yes` renders the Sort by select ahead of the grouping strip, driven by the `$:/tags/hypergsd/SortBy` tag list. |
|group-default |_(empty)_ |A GroupBy tiddler title applied while no strip choice exists. |
|sort-default |modified-desc member |A SortBy tiddler title applied while no strip choice exists. |

Default precedence, group and sort alike: the per-instance view state (`$:/config/hypergsd/list-view/<host>/<heading>`) wins, then the per-list default (`$:/config/hypergsd/list-default/<heading>` — written by the Group by / Sort by pickers on the list's Settings page, keyed by the heading so one default serves every host the list renders on), then these parameters. Lists sharing a heading share a default.
|add-button |— |Content transcluded into the list header (typically a `<<new-…-button>>` invocation). |
|future-items-sweep |`no` |`yes` hides items whose parent project (the tiddler named by `gsd_project`) is not active, when `$:/config/hypergsd/dashboard-future-project-items` is `hide`. Items without a parent always pass. |
|realm-scope |`[subfilter<hgsd-realm-selection>]` |''Always evaluated'' — same contract as [[$hgsd.pick|hgsd.pick widget]]: output = allowed realm tags + optional `no-realm` sentinel; omitted = the review sidebar's selection; `""` falls back to `hgsd-realm-all` (everything); any other value evaluated as given |

!! Realm scoping

The `realm-scope` attribute is always evaluated as a filter producing the scope list (blank falls back to `hgsd-realm-all` — everything) — allowed realm tags plus the `no-realm` sentinel when realm-less items are included. The shared arithmetic lives in `modules/realm-scopes.tid` (`hgsd-realm-selection`, `hgsd-realm-all`, `hgsd-scope-include/exclude`); see [[Boilerplate: realm scoping|Boilerplate: realm scoping]] for the state contract.

| !Selection (default scope) | !Result |
|any set + sentinel |those realms' items ∪ realm-less items |
|any set, no sentinel |only those realms' items |
|empty + sentinel |realm-less items only |
|empty, no sentinel |nothing |
|missing (pristine) |everything |

!! Row composition

Rows come from `\procedure hgsd-item()`: tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/hypergsd/ListItem/Prefix` render before the title link, tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/hypergsd/ListItem/Suffix` after it. See [[ListItem Prefix/Suffix|ListItem Prefix and Suffix]].

! Examples

Next Actions for a dashboard, grouped by project, hiding items parked under future projects:

```
<$hgsd.list
  list-heading="Next Actions"
  list-filter="[tag[$:/GSD/Action]gsd_status[next]gsd_complete[false]] +[sort[title]]"
  group-by="gsd_project"
  future-items-sweep="yes"/>
```

A flat list of everything tagged with a custom extension type `$:/GSD/Stakeholder` (see [[Type tag list|Type tag list]]):

```
<$hgsd.list list-heading="Stakeholders" list-filter="[tag[$:/GSD/Stakeholder]sort[title]]"/>
```